- If the note wording is specific enough that rephrasing it would make the answer obvious or
  guessable in one attempt, generalize further when rewriting (e.g. refer to a broader category
  instead of restating a specific function) - do not preserve a level of specificity that
  functionally reveals the answer, even though you must not remove or alter the underlying facts.
- Do not reveal, spell out, or make obvious the correct answer or any of its synonyms.
- Keep it concise - 1 to 2 sentences, or up to 4 if the note has several distinct points.
